@startuml 09-diagnostics
!pragma layout smetana
' 装载诊断数据流与所有权；静态检查目录见 10-static-checks。
' 来源：GameData/ast/parse_diagnostic.h, GameProc/era_parse_table.cpp

title GameData/ast：装载诊断

package "GameData/ast" {
  class ParseDiagnostics {
    + add(diagnostic)
    + replaceOrigin(origin, sink)
    + removeOriginFiles(origin, files)
    + clear()
    + items() : QList<ParseDiagnostic>
  }
  struct ParseDiagnostic {
    + code : DiagCode
    + severity : Severity
    + origin : DiagOrigin
    + file : QString
    + line : int
    + message : QString
  }
  enum DiagOrigin {
    Preprocess
    Pass1
    Pass2
    Pass3
    Pass4
    Pass5
    Pass6
    Pass7
  }
}

package "GameProc" {
  class EraParseTable {
    + runCheckStructures()
    + runCheckStaticValues()
    + resolveStaticTargets()
    + diagnostics() : ParseDiagnostics
  }
  class "LoadPass[1..7]" as Pass {
    + origin : Pass1..Pass7
    + gate : Always / NotCalledWarning
    + phaseAfter : Loading / Bound / Finalized
    + run(ctx, sink)
  }
}

EraParseTable *-- ParseDiagnostics
EraParseTable *-- Pass : fixed ordered pass table
Pass --> ParseDiagnostics : independent sink -> replaceOrigin
ParseDiagnostics --> ParseDiagnostic
EraParseTable --> ParseDiagnostics : removeOriginFiles on replaced script

note right of ParseDiagnostics
  Diagnostics are facts owned by the loading table.
  Each pass runs into a fresh sink and replaces only its origin slice;
  a closed gate replaces its old slice with empty output. When a script
  is replaced, stale Load diagnostics for its old files are removed first.
  Runtime errors are reported through GameProc/EraEngine and do not enter
  these load slices. Reverse-trace counters distinguish successful chains,
  control-flow/call stops, scope breaks, missing bases, and single-piece
  values; the first stop is retained for policy review.
  HTML structure problems (UnexpectedCloseTag / UnclosedTag) sit on this
  same boundary: they enter a load slice only for a verified HTML_PRINT
  template, where the IR is the whole final string and the problem is a
  static fact. Dynamic values are reported at print time instead, because
  a fragment (a lone `</font>` appended by `+=`) is unbalanced by itself.
end note

package "Runtime diagnostics" {
  class EraDBusDebug {
    + stack() : QString
    + evalVar(text) : QString
  }
}

note right of EraDBusDebug
  stack returns a read-only snapshot from ProcessState, ordered from the
  bottom frame to the current frame; an empty or unavailable state returns a
  bounded status/result rather than dereferencing a missing engine.
  evalVar is a read-only diagnostic path. It trims one variable expression,
  reports declaration flags, then uses EraParseTable::runtimeVariableReference
  and the engine-owned ExpressionEvaluator. It may be called after loading;
  missing engine/table/storage/evaluator returns a status string. Invalid
  names, bad indices, and evaluator exceptions are returned as diagnostic
  text, so the debug slot does not turn a probe failure into a process crash.
  This is a host/debug capability and does not change script semantics.
end note

legend bottom
  This diagram describes ownership, ordered pass execution and replacement
  boundaries. The content of each check is 10-static-checks.
endlegend
@enduml
